To isolate the combinatorics, collect the neighboring products into $K=\sum_{\langle x,x'\rangle}\phi(x)\phi(x').$ The corresponding factor in the path-integral weight is written schematically as $e^{-iK}.$ Its expansion is $e^{-iK}
=1-iK-\frac{1}{2!}K^2+\frac{i}{3!}K^3+\cdots,$ or, with the neighboring sums exposed, $\begin{aligned}
e^{-iK}
={}&1
-i\sum_{\langle x,x'\rangle}\phi(x)\phi(x')
\nonumber\\
&-\frac{1}{2!}
\sum_{\langle x,x'\rangle}
\sum_{\langle y,y'\rangle}
\phi(x)\phi(x')\phi(y)\phi(y')
+\cdots .\end{aligned}$ Each factor independently selects a neighboring pair.

